    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "# MiniMax H3 video in a 360 panorama room\n\nThe panorama is turned into a sheet of camera views, and the sheet is the only reference image\n(`<Picture 1>`) of MiniMax H3 reference-to-video.\n\n## Models (in `ComfyUI/models/`)\n| File | Folder |\n|---|---|\n| minimax_h3_ref2va_pruned_int8_convrot.safetensors | diffusion_models |\n| qwen3vl_32b_minimax_h3_nvfp4_awq.safetensors | text_encoders |\n| minimax_h3_video_vae_fp16.safetensors | vae |\n| minimax_h3_audio_vae_fp32.safetensors | vae |\n\nAll from [Comfy-Org/MiniMax-H3](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MiniMax-H3).\n\nCustom nodes: this pack, and ComfyUI-KJNodes for the memory-efficient attention patch (without it the\nrender is many times slower on a low-VRAM setup).\n\n## Use\n1. Load the panorama.\n2. Rewrite the prompt for your room and shot: see `skills/h3-location-prompting/SKILL.md`. The prompt in\n   the workflow is an example for a dark seaside living room.\n3. Test at 0.2 megapixels and 5 s, then raise megapixels and duration.\n\nKeep `ref_image_size` on `max` (with `match` the sheet is shrunk to the video size and the views lose\ntheir detail) and CFG at 1. The shot should start from where the panorama was taken.\n"
   ],
   "title": "What to download / how to use"
  }
